{"name":"Zinfandel Red","hex":"#5a3844","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zinfandel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dry red wine of California.","A small black grape from which zinfandel wine is made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zinfandel"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zinfandel","blocks":[{"text":"Zinfandel is a variety of black-skinned wine grape. The variety is grown in over 10 percent of California vineyards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Ripe_Zinfandel_grapes_in_Dry_Creek_Valley-8958.jpg/330px-Ripe_Zinfandel_grapes_in_Dry_Creek_Valley-8958.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zinfandel"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia